### VideoFingerprinter (M1-13)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.hash.VideoFingerprinter`, `DHash`, `VideoContentMatcher`, `VideoFingerprintCodec`; injectable `VideoFrameExtractor`; `AndroidVideoMetadataReader` on StatStage for video rows.
- **iOS:** `DBVideoFingerprinter`, `DBDHash`, `DBVideoContentMatcher`, `DBVideoFingerprint` under `ScanEngine/Hash/`.
- **Pipeline:** Video files hash `RAW_BYTES` + `VIDEO_CONTENT_V1` in parallel (`HashResult.VideoSuccess` / `DBHashPipelineOutcomeVideoSuccess`); >500 MB without opt-in skips content fingerprint (`VideoPartialSuccess`).
- **Caps:** 90 s wall-clock, 500 MB budget (2 GB with `largeFilesOptIn`), 5-frame dHash at 2/25/50/75/98% (single frame <3 s), Hamming ≤8 default, duration gate (2% and <1 s delta).
- **Index:** `fingerprint_id` = VIDEO_CONTENT_V1, `raw_content_fingerprint_id` = RAW_BYTES on `file_entry`; `frame_hashes_blob` on fingerprint row (debug-only egress).
- **Grouper:** EXACT_BYTES via `raw_content_fingerprint_id`; SAME_CONTENT_VIDEO via `fingerprint_id` profile; fuzzy Hamming clustering for M1-18 fixture suite uses `VideoContentMatcher`.
- **Tests:** `DHashTest`, `VideoFingerprinterTest`, `VideoContentMatcherTest`, `VideoFingerprintCodecTest` / iOS `DBVideoFingerprinterTests`, `DBVideoContentMatcherTests`; fixture `hash-video-content-01.json`.
- **Platform decode (Android):** `ContentResolverVideoFrameExtractor` via `MediaMetadataRetriever` frame sampling (same stack as `AndroidVideoMetadataReader`); `VideoFingerprinter` wired in `ScanOrchestratorFactory`.
- **Backfill:** `IndexWriter.listVideoContentBackfillEntries` + `ScanOrchestrator.backfillVideoContentFingerprints` before grouping (RAW-only video rows from pre-wiring scans).

### ImageFingerprinter (M3-12)

- **Android:** `ImageFingerprinter`, `ImageContentMatcher`, `ContentResolverImageBitmapExtractor` — single-frame dHash (≤320×180) parallel with `RAW_BYTES`; `IMAGE_CONTENT_V1` on `fingerprint_id`.
- **Decode:** Rewind FD before second `BitmapFactory` pass; apply EXIF orientation; scale to ≤320×180 before dHash (recompressed Downloads exports).
- **Hamming:** Image ship threshold **10** (FR-FP-09 QA budget) — not video’s 8 — for heavy recompression false-negatives (e.g. `download.jpeg` vs `images.jpeg`).
- **Size-bucket:** Images always `NEEDS_HASH` (like video) so unique-size re-encodes still get perceptual fingerprint (fixes missed recompressed dupes).
- **Backfill:** `IndexWriter.listImageContentBackfillEntries` + `ScanOrchestrator.backfillImageContentFingerprints` before grouping — re-hash legacy size-bucket skips and RAW_BYTES-only image rows missing `IMAGE_CONTENT_V1`.
- **Grouper:** Fuzzy union-find on dHash Hamming ≤10 → `SAME_CONTENT_IMAGE`; mixed raw → `SAME_CONTENT_IMAGE`, all same raw → `EXACT_BYTES` (AC-equiv-image-content-04).
- **Grouper (video):** Fuzzy union-find via `VideoContentMatcher.contentMatches` (duration gate + ≥3/5 frames Hamming ≤8) → `SAME_CONTENT_VIDEO`; all same `raw_content_fingerprint_id` → `EXACT_BYTES` (AC-equiv-video-xres-04). Replaces exact-`fingerprint_id`-only video grouping.
- **UI:** `SAME_CONTENT_IMAGE` uses `match.imageContent.*`, `ContentMatchNotice`, `MatchKindBadge` caution surface; `IMAGE_DECODE_FAILED` in unscan tokens.
- **iOS:** `DBImageFingerprinter`, `DBImageContentMatcher`, `DBUiImageBitmapExtractor`, rewritten `DBGrouper` (fuzzy video+image clustering), `DBScanOrchestrator.backfillImageContentFingerprints`, `DBScanOrchestratorFactory` production wiring.
- **Tests:** `ImageContentMatcherTest`, `GrouperImageContentTest`, `DBImageContentMatcherTests`, `DBGrouperImageContentTests`; extended `DBScanOrchestratorTests` (toctou/tombstone/grant-revoke/resume); rescan required after upgrade.

### Video pipeline exception (M1-14)

- **Android:** `DurationBucketIndex`, `InMemoryDurationBucketIndex`, `SqliteDurationBucketIndex`; `HashPipeline` runs duration pre-bucket before size-bucket for video.
- **iOS:** `DBDurationBucketIndex`, `DBInMemoryDurationBucketIndex`, `DBSqliteDurationBucketIndex`; same ordering in `DBHashPipeline`.
- **Size-bucket skip:** Video never size-bucket-skips (`SizeBucketIndex` / `DBSizeBucketIndex` always `NEEDS_HASH`); `countIndexedFilesWithSize` excludes rows with `duration_ms > 0`.
